<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;Hi lbe,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yes, &lt;c&gt;$cell || next;&lt;/c&gt; is yet another one to add to the list of ways to do it :-) (Although it's probably easier to get bitten by precedence issues on that one so personally, I'd avoid it.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;c&gt;if (...) {...}&lt;/c&gt; is definitely what I'd use if the condition or the statement becomes more complex. For example, I've often written code something like &lt;c&gt;if ($x &amp;&amp; $y) { warn "skipping b/c foo"; next }&lt;/c&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Regards,&lt;br&gt;-- Hauke D&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
